Ansible Tags

🔹 PHASE 4: Advanced Ansible
Today I learned about Ansible Tags, which help in running only specific tasks instead of executing the entire Playbook 🎯
This is very useful in large automation projects where running full Playbooks every time is not efficient.
 Tags make automation faster, flexible, and more controlled ⚡

🔹 🏷️ Running Selective Tasks
Tags allow us to execute only selected tasks in a Playbook.

Example:
- name: Install nginx
 apt:
 name: nginx
 state: present
 tags: install

Run only tagged tasks using:
ansible-playbook playbook.yml --tags install
This saves time and avoids unnecessary task execution 🚀

🔹 📊 Tag Strategies
Good tag strategies improve Playbook management in real projects.
Common tagging approaches:
 • install → for installation tasks
 • config → for configuration tasks
 • deploy → for deployment tasks
 • restart → for service-related tasks
Proper tagging makes automation modular and easier to maintain 📦

🔹 ⏭️ Skipping Tasks
Ansible also allows skipping specific tagged tasks.
Command:
ansible-playbook playbook.yml --skip-tags install

This is useful when:
 • You want to avoid risky tasks
 • Skip long-running steps
 • Run only safe updates
Skipping tasks gives better control over execution flow 🔄

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Tags enable selective task execution.
 Smart tagging improves automation control.
 Skip or run tasks based on operational needs.
